{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Then I stationed two thanksgiving choirs.</b> So they are called because they stand to give thanks to HaShem, and they are the ones who sing a song of thanksgiving." "<b>And processions.</b> A noun on the pattern of תנחומות, and it is from the root הלך. The meaning: that he stationed the men of the thanksgiving choirs to go toward the right side."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:39.048986406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}